<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore Airlines says may list units.</title>
<headline>Singapore Airlines says may list units.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore Airlines Ltd does not rule out listing one or more of its subsidiaries eventually although it will not do so within the year, the Business Times said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The daily quoted an SIA spokesman as saying the company had no plans to list any of its units in the forseeable future because it had &quot;no good reason to do so&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;However, this does not mean we never shall,&quot; the spokesman was quoted as saying. &quot;We are not against the principle of listing subsidiaries.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
